WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.220
VIKI Agent is a proactive coding agent

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.240
with a decision engine that chooses when to
help,

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.570
what to suggest, and which work may start.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.060
It brings Claude Code and your Markdown
project knowledge together,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.970
so a useful next step can reach you before
you ask.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.130
With proactivity enabled and the app open,

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.830
it considers your goals, context, timing,
and granted authority.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:32.930
It can stay quiet, surface a suggestion, or
start eligible work.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:40.500
Your vault provides durable goals, tasks,
sources, and decisions.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.580
VIKI turns that context into opportunities
to move your project forward.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.170
That includes proposing work beyond your
task list.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.530
After repeated API reviews,

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.650
VIKI offers to turn that workflow into a
reusable skill.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.920
The launcher explains why and links to the
source chats.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.810
Make this a skill prepares an unsent message
for your review.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.300
Other offers help you learn from captured
sources,

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.070
run a retrospective, or improve Decision
questions.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.610
These proposals stay in your hands.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.370
Now follow a separate coding task from
context to result.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:20.980
A due vault task asks for positive checkout
quantities.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.920
Ask first reserves mission starts for you.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.690
Allowed lets eligible work begin within your
activity limits.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.320
On its next decision cycle,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.360
VIKI starts without another chat prompt.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.990
The agent reads the task and code, then
requests an edit.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.780
Independent work still respects native
permissions:

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.500
Allow once approves the edit,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.120
and running the test command needs a
separate approval.

00:01:44.193 --> 00:01:45.843
The agent responses are scripted;

00:01:45.863 --> 00:01:49.713
the app workflow, disposable edit, and local
checks are real.

00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:51.953
You can follow what happened and review the
evidence

00:01:51.953 --> 00:01:53.471
before deciding what comes next.

00:01:53.631 --> 00:01:56.201
Your responses also shape future decisions.

00:01:56.321 --> 00:01:58.371
Opening a suggestion, acting on it,

00:01:58.411 --> 00:02:01.021
or choosing Not useful gives VIKI feedback.

00:02:01.581 --> 00:02:03.261
With enough labeled decisions,

00:02:03.281 --> 00:02:05.441
local learning adapts the scoring weights;

00:02:05.651 --> 00:02:07.571
attention estimates also adjust.

00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:09.731
Learning shows what changed,

00:02:09.931 --> 00:02:13.461
the starting and current values, and the
evidence behind them.

00:02:14.101 --> 00:02:15.961
You can turn it off or reset it.

00:02:15.961 --> 00:02:20.186
This adapts VIKI's decisions, without
retraining Claude.

00:02:20.186 --> 00:02:23.781
Broader improvements to skills, knowledge,
and Decision questions

00:02:23.781 --> 00:02:25.831
begin as drafts for review.

00:02:25.951 --> 00:02:30.091
Sensitive instruction and system files are
excluded from knowledge upkeep.

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:32.661
The optional starter supplies deny rules;

00:02:32.661 --> 00:02:36.171
your configured Claude Code hooks can block
covered operations.

00:02:36.171 --> 00:02:40.121
Discover useful work. Delegate with control.

00:02:40.141 --> 00:02:42.531
Learn from the outcome. VIKI Agent.
